Yeah, ri'usri seems like a good generic word for "strap" (i.e. it could work
in situations where you want to say "seat belt" AND in situations where you
want "luggage strap").  One could then get more specific and say
{preri'usri} or {bafri'usri} if the situation requires that level of
specificity.

